# NATHAN AI — HOP IN. / Five-Matrix Worlds

This **additive** module joins the pre-existing Hop In chatbox and its seven intact lenses, 104 A–Z feature ideas, and 43 originally enumerated settings. It opens from the new **Five Matrices** tool panel as a full-screen accessible dialog, or in a separate app view.

## Working modes
- **Atlas:** the exact existing **103-object baseline** imported without alteration as JSON, joined additively with **50 companion teaching records** (153 indexed rows, including overlapping subjects). Search by name, source universe and five-matrix axis; source objects retain their original classifications.
- **Educational quest:** 15 source-identified, auto-graded questions with scorekeeping and answer explanations.
- **Book Series Workshop:** 15 original companion-volume **outlines** across three series; save a working book starter in Markdown and optionally send a chapter-development prompt back to the Hop In composer. No completed novels are claimed.
- **Learning Laboratory:** Five lens lessons, cross-linked source examples, and an interactive twelve-ring **symbolic** body-position selector with a JSON export.
- **Original Words:** On-demand search over two byte-preserved conversation source attachments and the exact index from the connected FIVE-MATRIX Source Atlas. The entire owner's past chats are not included without source files.

The five matrices are **BODY, SOUL, SHADOW, MIND, SPIRIT**. The separate seven-coordinate conceptual tensor **Natural, Soul, Spirit, Shadow, Dead, Alive, Mind** is not collapsed into five labels.

## The other app
Authoritative original words, line-level indexing and the fifteen formulas live in:
\`app-factory/one/five-matrix-atlas/\`.

The Hop In module uses relative paths to these same assets; it does **not duplicate** or modify the original sources. The classifications and comparisons are assistant-written educational metadata. Biblical references, Tolkien/Lewis fictional canon, and user-supplied symbolic claims are distinct.

## Source permissions and factual boundaries
The project is publicly hosted in GitHub. Do not import private chat exports or copyrighted novel text into this public working tree without source and rights review. Existing attachments are conversations, with mixed author/assistant turns; the complete originals are preserved, but not all lines are solely user-written. Original book and film universes are credited to their respective authors. A twelve-ring design does not establish supernatural effects. Simulation does not establish quantum-hardware functionality or infallible truth detection.

## Launch and tests

\`\`\`sh
python3 -m http.server 8765
# open http://localhost:8765/app-factory/nathan-ai/hop-in/chatbox/
node --test app-factory/nathan-ai/hop-in/chatbox/engine.test.cjs
node --test app-factory/nathan-ai/hop-in/chatbox/five-matrix/engine.test.cjs
\`\`\`

All existing chatbox functions remain in \`../app.js\`, \`../engine.js\`, and their source catalogs. The new dialog bridge sends only a user-reviewed prompt into the existing chat composer; **it never auto-sends to a model or provider**.

